====Adjective====
{{en-adj|?}}

# Of or relating to social [[outcast]]s.
# Of or relating to the [[lumpenproletariat]].
# [[plebeian|Plebeian]].
# [[lump|Lump]]-like.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000 |title=The Limits of Death: Between Philosophy and Psychoanalysis  |author=Joanne Morra, ‎Mark Robson, ‎& Marquard Smith  |page=72 |ISBN=0719057515 |passage=This something, which is neither body nor machine but interior and alien to them both, pertains to the 'meat' in Gibson's world insofar as the 'meat' - that useless corporeal remainder discarded by the machine - retains an excess that cannot be reduced to the '''lumpen''' mass of fleshy existence. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|title=Texts and Contexts: Introducing Literature and Language Study |author=Adrian Beard  |page= |ISBN=0415229871 |passage=Using the last two as an example, there is a constant sense of contrast in the poem, in this case between the streamlined ship which will surge through the water and the mere '''lumpen''' shape of the clumsy iceberg. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|title=A Grave Denied |author=Dana Stabenow |page=17 |ISBN=0312985649 |passage=Billy and Dandy had draped a tarp over the body but the shape itself looked '''lumpen''' and grotesque. }}

